# 0002. A static one-page site: LESS for styles, jQuery for behaviour

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-19

The site is one HTML page with sections and anchor navigation, styles written in LESS and
compiled to one CSS file, and jQuery plugins for the slider and the reservation form.

## Technical details
- **Page** (`www/index.html`): fixed header menu linking to `#section-head`, `-info`,
  `-gallery`, `-reserve`, `-contacts`.
- **Styles**: `www/public/less/main.less` imports `reset`, `font`, `btn`, `layout`; the
  compiled `www/public/css/main.css` is committed and loaded by the page. Exo 2 web fonts in
  four weights.
- **Scripts** (`www/public/js/main.js`): menu behaviour, FlexSlider gallery, and an AJAX
  POST of `#reserve-form` to `index.php`, expecting JSON `{result: 1}`; the PHP back end was
  never committed. Contacts use a Google Maps script.
- **Repo layout**: `trunk/` and `branches/` mimic an SVN layout from the course; the git
  branches `img`, `js` (merged) and `css` (one commit) were the git half of the exercise.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: HTML5, LESS, jQuery 2.1.4, FlexSlider, Google Maps JS.
- Alternatives: plain CSS (LESS gave variables and nesting); a static site generator (more
  than one page needs).
